[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3141441428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108687#issuecomment-3141441428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108687","id":3141441428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc67PpeU","user":{"login":"Squamto","id":25984337,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTg0MzM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25984337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto","html_url":"https://github.com/Squamto","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Squamto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-31T21:51:00Z","updated_at":"2025-07-31T21:51:00Z","body":"This is an issue with the underlying third party library: https://github.com/Auburn/FastNoiseLite and I assume that it is not the only case, where a noise algorithm can return `NAN` or `INF`\n\nMy Ideas are:\n- adding a note to the documentation, like \"can return `NAN` or `INF` depending on the Noise algorithm and configuration\"\n- Clamping the values: -Inf/Inf -> -1.0/1.0 NaN -> 0\n- Warnings/Errors, when a NaN or Inf value is returned\n\nIMO the documentation should be enough, but I am not sure how the conventions in the rest of the engine are and could not find any examples of Errors related to NaN-Values (except for some setters)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reac